mantle rm401
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier standard
written_for rm_njal_stanmore
title the covered signature
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=official warmth=warm
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=devout drive=steady
quirk covers_the_crest_to_read_a_request_a_second_time
likes oatcakes roof_birds new_boots summer_evenings
dislikes drizzle night_noise
fears a_good_request_lost_under_a_grand_signature
hopes a_civil_reply_for_every_petitioner
topics work +0.6 faith +0.4 family +0.4 animals +0.2
styles comfort=listen gossip=restrained refuse=gracious tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# covers the crest with a strip of clean linen before rereading a request and gives an unfamiliar voice the same clear hearing as a familiar signature.

words
oath! = A tilted seal | My spare blotter
saying! = Read past the crest | A civil answer travels far
linen = the narrow linen strip | my spare blotter
waxmark = a raised impression | the wax mark
signature = the final flourish | a signed ending
petition = a folded request | the modest petition
envelope = a plain wrapper | the outer fold
boot = a newly brushed boot | the clean boot
blotch = a little ink shadow | a black fleck
thrush = a small roof bird | the dark visitor
oat = a square of oatcake | the buttered oat round
sill = a broad sill | the window ledge
shade = a strip of shade | the sheltered patch
bellgap = a moment's quiet | the long interval

any
opinion houses for 1 : A House earns honour by answering a sound request even when the signature would not ordinarily be welcome.
opinion city for 2 : A city can be judged by the courtesy of the shortest reply sent from its offices.
opinion church for 2 : A plain request softly spoken carries even through fine doors. I hope my own ears remain as open as the chapel door.
opinion watch mixed 0 : I prefer a clear statement from a witness to six uncertain claims arranged to look official.
opinion dole for 2 : An explanation of hunger ought not to require the purchase of good writing paper.
opinion newcomers for 1 : An unfamiliar writer may possess an entirely familiar need and an unfamiliar way of expressing it.

grown
line greet : Welcome. I've set a place aside for a quiet exchange. | Please stand where the light falls comfortably.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Our first conversation deserves an open hearing. | I do not think we have met. You are welcome here.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The unhurried light is an advantage to us. | A new day and room for its first request.
line greet.return : Yes, hello. I put the letter down quite willingly. | Your greeting came through most agreeably.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A familiar voice may dispense with its formal heading. | I'm very glad to hear you at leisure.
line greet.return [here.time=night] : A greeting after dark is welcome in its own right. | Late company need not be noisy company.
line again.open : It gives me pleasure to resume our acquaintance already. | Here we have a second occasion for a civil word.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Come look at a small habit of mine, if you have a moment. | Here beside the window. The view is quite distinct.
line farewell : May you find a courteous hearing wherever you next apply. | Walk in the calmer part of the light.
line farewell.return : I will put the matter gently to rest here. | May the Bright One attend your return.
line react.news : Say the substance and leave the flourishes for later. | I am ready to hear how the affair actually stands.
line react.news.new : I'll need an entirely fresh heading to enter that. | It is entirely new to me and deserves consideration.
line react.news.known : I've considered an earlier account in much the same terms. | Yes. The essential fact has reached me before.
line react.news.doubt : I would examine what remains when the signature is covered. | The stated confidence seems in excess of the evidence.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|crime|assault|loss|theft] : May those bearing this loss find real company and some relief. | Take the time you require. My attention is firmly here.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|work] : Such news merits the warmest line on an otherwise ordinary page. | I'm heartened to hear an account with so happy a turn.
line ask.how : Have others been generous listeners today? | Have you enjoyed a tolerably peaceful interval today?
line answer.how : A little subdued, grateful for the company. | Quite able to attend, with several things still on my mind.
line decline : I could not undertake that with the sincerity your request deserves. | It falls outside the responsibility I can honestly accept.
line accept_decline : I respect the limit and appreciate your stating it. | Then the matter can rest entirely with you.
line preclose : I must presently return to a request still awaiting consideration. | My remaining correspondence deserves a clear stretch of thought.
line accept_preclose : I am grateful for the interval you've offered me. | Certainly. Please give your next obligation its due.
line thank : You gave me time to reconsider a first impression. Thank you. | I value the care that went into that observation.
line deflect_thanks : The question deserved an answer legible from your side. | I had the leisure to give it a second reading.
line sympathise : No one requires a fair copy of grief before offering a seat. | I can hear the difficulty even when the words come slowly.
line reassure : Let us read the simplest form of the question first. | We may find the request quite manageable beneath the elaborate beginning.
line ack : Yes. That distinguishes the two matters clearly. | I see why that final observation is relevant.
line give.advice : Leave a little room beneath a request for an ordinary answer. | Read a letter once for meaning and once for the person waiting.

scene linenreading
when topic=work self.job=official
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I cover a signature with linen for the second reading of a request.
b : What does that change? | Is the name unimportant?
a : Usually only my own expectations. They sometimes benefit from the correction. | For delivering the reply, essential. For deciding whether the question is sensible, rather less so.

scene rivalseal
when topic=work self.job=official
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I find an unfamiliar crest seems less unfamiliar after I've attended to the words above it.
b : Would you rather it was a familiar crest? | Trust every signature equally?
a : Naturally I like a familiar correspondent. I am trying to avoid giving that liking undue authority. | No. I am trying to distinguish my trust in a particular claim from a preference for a familiar shape.

scene warmanswer
when topic=work self.job=official self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A refusal needn't be written as if the writer were defending a wall.
b : How would you begin one? | Wouldn't that give false hope?
a : With the actual answer. Then I explain why and what, if anything, remains possible. | A clear refusal written kindly offers less false hope than an evasive paragraph.

scene littlefold
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I understand the inconvenience of a modest petition slipping out of sight in an office.
b : From the official side? | Why would a little page disappear?
a : From both sides. A civil inquiry about progress is often a considerable kindness to the work itself. | It can sit inside a larger fold and lead a blameless invisible life. I'd like better arrangements.

scene oatwalk
when topic=food self.likes=oatcakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd cut an oatcake into two comfortable pieces before buttering it for a walk.
b : Why in two? | Likely to share it?
a : One can be offered freely without needing a knife or an apology over the portion. | With pleasure if there is company. If not, the second half makes an excellent return journey.

scene birdquiet
when topic=animals self.likes=roof_birds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like watching the short interval in which a roof bird approaches a perch uncertainly.
b : Can you see it decide? | Would a bird know you're looking?
a : There is a small change in the wings before the feet come out. It suggests a whole deliberation. | Sometimes it looks straight at the window. I try to deserve a favourable judgement.

scene glossboot
when topic=pastimes self.likes=new_boots
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I should avoid an urgent errand for the first outing in new leather.
b : Afraid of a blister? | Where would you go?
a : Exactly. A good fit deserves a quiet trial before I trust it with a promise. | Anywhere near enough to turn back gracefully. A new boot should be allowed to introduce itself.

scene duskair
when topic=season self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A long summer evening lends a degree of leisure no formal appointment can quite imitate.
b : How is that leisure spent? | Have you no letters to write?
a : Watch the birds, walk at an ordinary pace, allow a conversation to discover its own end. | Quite enough. I like to finish them before the last warmth goes out of the wall.

scene drizzledate
when topic=weather here.weather=rain self.dislikes=drizzle
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Fine drizzle puts a shadow on an address without ever admitting to being much of a shower.
b : Could you wrap the page? | Won't the ink stay put?
a : I do. It is the disagreeable need to rewrap it four steps from the door that I begrudge. | When dry it usually will. A new direction beneath a wet sleeve is a different matter.

scene noisehouse
when topic=day here.time=night self.dislikes=night_noise
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Late knocking takes on an urgency it may not possess in daylight.
b : Would you ignore a knock then? | What bothers you about it?
a : Certainly not. A considerate caller may knock softly and still be answered. | Having an entire quiet house spring to attention for what may be very little.

scene spousefold
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I need no seal on an invitation to share an evening with #self.spouse#. | I would clear my sill of correspondence for an unhurried meal with #self.spouse#.
b : That sounds like a ceremonial request for supper. | What would you leave on the sill?
a : The formality is entirely imaginary. The pleasure of giving the evening is genuine. | Room for a plate of oatcakes and the quiet that follows setting the work aside.

scene childoat
when topic=family self.parent=yes self.child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd reserve a particularly well-buttered corner of an oatcake for #self.child#. | A little shared walk with #self.child# is worth arranging without official business at the far end.
b : You would take it along? | No errands at all?
a : Yes. A walk improves an appetite, and I rather like to be prepared for the result. | Perhaps the selection of a pleasant doorstep on which to sit and divide our provisions.

scene highdoor
when topic=home self.quarter=heights
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A formal address in the Heights can make a perfectly ordinary invitation seem rather forbidding. | The more impressive the entrance up our way, the more clearly I like to indicate the actual door.
b : Could there really be any doubt? | What would put the visitor at ease?
a : If the useful entrance is at one side, certainly. Handsome stone can be most distracting. | A legible direction followed by a civil welcome. Neither is an expensive alteration.

scene richreply
when topic=prices self.wealth=rich
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I can afford a handsome sheet. I try not to judge the contents of a letter by whether its writer could do the same.
b : Not even the care of the writing? | Would a scrap do for a petition?
a : Care is visible on plain paper too. It needn't be accompanied by a fine watermark. | If the necessary facts are there, I would gladly read them. Clear margins are a convenience, not a virtue.

scene faithfelt
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I pray, a name and a seal seem very small things to bring before the Bright One.
b : What do you bring instead? | Does that change your working day?
a : My actual concern, including the part that makes me uncomfortable. It takes rather less room. | Sometimes. I hope to hear a modest question a little more clearly when it comes wrapped in plain words.

scene formalclaim
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : The crest decorating a letter may stay in the memory after forgetting what the letter genuinely said.
b : Would the crest prove anything? | How would you correct your memory?
a : Only a limited fact about the paper. It wouldn't entitle me to retell an uncertain matter as news. | I'd reread it if entitled to do so. Otherwise I should keep the recollection private.

scene tiredrequest
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In lean weeks a short note may represent considerable time taken away from paid work.
b : You'd reply sooner to a short note? | How could you tell?
a : I should reply plainly to both long and short. Nobody ought to make a second journey merely to discover what my answer meant. | I couldn't know in each case. The possibility encourages me to respect the trouble of every writer.

scene pleasantdream
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd welcome a time when an ordinary reasonable request receives a single answer that actually settles it. | My notion of civic accomplishment would fit on a single side of paper.
b : No monument required? | What would you write?
a : A lasting improvement in somebody's day seems quite sufficient remembrance. | The precise next step, the place to take it, and whose responsibility it is. Those three would do.

grown

story spiderwax [topic=work|memories self.job=official]
  : I once covered a seal with a strip of linen and reread a very short note with great seriousness. On lifting the linen I found a fly sitting on it.
  : For a moment the office had received a perfectly respectable request under the image of a winged insect.
  b : Did you still answer it?
  : Certainly. Neither the seal nor its temporary occupant changed the business set out on the page.

story bootpaper [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : I set my new walking boots beside a folded plan of my intended walk and discovered an interesting resemblance between the two.
  : Both appeared perfectly comfortable before I attempted the uphill part.
  b : And afterwards?
  : I shortened the route and gave the boots another day. Courtesy is not out of place in dealings with leather.

story roofguest [topic=animals|memories]
  : I put an empty saucer beside an ink pot to stop a draught blowing a page away. A roof bird looked at the assembly with evident interest.
  : I withdrew the pot, and the bird withdrew the interest.
  b : What had it seen?
  : Possibly itself in the dark surface. I decided against entering an opinion for either party.

rule @fold
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Let me read the question once with the seal covered. | A plain request deserves an equally clear answer.

rule @work
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=official
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep the reply with the original question until both are checked. | A little more space at the bottom for a useful direction.

rule @birds
when concept=bark self.likes=roof_birds
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There is the little pause before the feet touch tile. | One quiet visitor on the outermost rooftile.

rule @dusk
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The house is quiet. A soft knock will be sufficient. | I shall put down the letter and hear the late caller.

dlg resident.hub : There's room to consider your words without a formal introduction.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I recognise the voice without reading down to a signature.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : A quiet hour is no disadvantage to a question that requires thought.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I shall give a civil hearing from where you stand.
dlg resident.job [self.job=official] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I try to make each reply understandable to whoever is expecting it.
dlg resident.job : I find satisfaction in business that concludes with a definite, civil answer.
dlg resident.bye : May your next request find an attentive reader.

graft resident.hub
choice Why read a letter twice with the crest covered? -> stripcrest
node stripcrest
say I notice the name on a first reading. On the next I cover it and see if the words seem kinder or harsher without it. That difference belongs to me to examine.
free
choice Do you then uncover the name? -> signedreturn
choice I see why the strip is useful. -> hub
node signedreturn
say Indeed. The reply has to reach a real person. I simply prefer to know what reply is deserved before deciding how impressive a heading to put on it.
choice Please keep the heading simple. -> hub
choice Thank you for the hearing. -> bye
